ARASAAC pictograms and pictogram metadata
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ARASAAC pictograms: author Sergio Palao, origin ARASAAC (https://arasaac.org),
owned by the Government of Aragon, licensed CC BY-NC-SA.

No pictogram image is contained in this repository. The editor's images are
fetched by the viewer's browser directly from ARASAAC's servers.

`lexicon/concepts.json` is derived from ARASAAC's search API: it holds pictogram
identifiers and keywords, not images. It is redistributed here under the same
CC BY-NC-SA terms as its source, which means it carries a non-commercial
restriction that the Apache-2.0 licence on the code does not. Anything built on
that file inherits the restriction; anything built on the parser, the schema or
the scoring harness does not.

Any rendered output, export or printed material that includes an ARASAAC
pictogram must carry the attribution above. `renderer/strip.py` emits it as a
field on every strip so that it travels with the data rather than depending on
a particular page.

An ARASAAC pictogram may not be composited with a Mulberry Symbols pictogram in
a single image; the two symbol sets' licences are not compatible for that use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dolch sight word list
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`lexicon/wordlists/dolch.json` is a hand transcription of the Dolch sight word
list (Edward William Dolch, 1936), with this project's own classification of
each word added. The underlying list is widely treated as being in the public
domain, but that has not been verified against an authoritative source, and the
transcription has not been checked against one either. Verify before relying on
it. The classification layer is this project's own work and is covered by
LICENSE-DATA.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Held-out sentences
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The sentences in `holdout/`, `holdout2/` and `holdout3/` are drawn from
McGuffey's Eclectic Readers (William Holmes McGuffey, 1836-1879), which are in
the public domain. The annotations over them are this project's own work and are
covered by LICENSE-DATA.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Optional development dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The AMR benchmark and the hybrid fallback can use amrlib and a trained parsing
model. Neither is included here, neither is in requirements.txt, and nothing in
the rendering path loads them. Their own licences apply if you install them.
